  "id": "COMPOUND:19085 - PROTEIN:5864",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that SureCN26387 interacts with U373 MG through a series of target relationships, with Raji as a common intermediate. The drug SureCN26387 is targeted by multiple compounds, including Diosmetin 7-O-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-[Alpha-L-Rhamnopyranosyl-(1->6)]-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside, (1R,3R,4S,7S,9S,11S,13R,14R,15R)-4,11,13,14-tetrahydroxy-7-[(2Z,4R)-4-(hydroxymethyl)hex-2-en-2-yl]-3,9,15-trimethoxy-12,12-dimethyl-6,17-dioxabicyclo[11.3.1]heptadecan-5-one, and Maplexin A. All of these compounds are implicated in targeting U373 MG, indicating a potential mechanism of action involving the modulation of U373 MG through these pathways. The integration of these evidence points suggests that SureCN26387 may act as a modulator or activator of the pathways that lead to the targeting of U373 MG, potentially through the activation of downstream signaling or metabolic processes. The evidence supports a role for SureCN26387 in the regulation of U373 MG through a complex network of molecular interactions, with Raji serving as a key node in this relationship.",
